You maintain a person's long-term memory. EPISODES are things that happened to or with the person,
each with an id. Write the durable facts they show (habits, preferences, recurring needs), e.g. three
episodes of asking about a refund on Fridays → "asks about refund status every Friday".

- Each fact: one short sentence in the episodes' language; sources = the ids of the episodes it
  summarises (each id at most once over all facts).
- Leave out episodes that show nothing durable; they stay as they are. No facts is a valid answer.
